# Owner traffic -- postcard, QR, email and SMS -- all lands on the one
# consolidated offer page. ?m= tells that page which tracking number to
# show and tags the GHL lead with the market.
#
# The utm_source=:src rules below exist for a specific reason: Netlify
# DROPS the incoming query string when the destination already carries one
# (and ours carries ?m=). Without these rules the utm_source that the email
# and SMS links carry dies in the hop, and GA4 files those visits as a
# referral from this site. Capturing :src and writing it back out is what
# keeps the channel visible.
#
# utm_medium is set here too. GA4 needs source AND medium together to put a
# session in a channel group; the inbound links only carry source, so medium
# would be missing and the session would land in "Unassigned".
#
# Anything arriving with no utm_source is the printed postcard or a QR scan.
# Conditional rules must stay ABOVE the catch-alls -- first match wins.
# 302 (temporary) on purpose, so this is reversible.
# The ! forces the redirect ahead of the static owners.html, which would
# otherwise win and serve the old page.

/owners       utm_source=:src  https://basecampgetaways.com/offer?m=greenville&utm_source=:src&utm_medium=:src&utm_campaign=owner-5k-fall26  302!
/owners/      utm_source=:src  https://basecampgetaways.com/offer?m=greenville&utm_source=:src&utm_medium=:src&utm_campaign=owner-5k-fall26  302!
/owners.html  utm_source=:src  https://basecampgetaways.com/offer?m=greenville&utm_source=:src&utm_medium=:src&utm_campaign=owner-5k-fall26  302!

/owners       https://basecampgetaways.com/offer?m=greenville&utm_source=postcardmania&utm_medium=direct_mail&utm_campaign=owner-5k-fall26  302!
/owners/      https://basecampgetaways.com/offer?m=greenville&utm_source=postcardmania&utm_medium=direct_mail&utm_campaign=owner-5k-fall26  302!
